Apple's second-generation <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> will retain its existing display sizes and side-mounted fingerprint sensor, according to the leaker known as "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/digital-chat-station/">Digital Chat Station</a>."<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/09/face-id.jpg" alt="" width="1023" height="573" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-966000" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://weibo.com/6048569942/5366599876871054">new post</a> on Weibo, the leaker said information about the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; 2 remains limited, but engineering units continue to feature a 7.6-inch inner display, a 5.4-inch outer display, and a fingerprint sensor on the side, with no clear sign of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a> being added to the device. Those details carry over the screen sizes and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> arrangement of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-announces-foldable-iphone-duo/">first-generation model</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Digital Chat Station also questioned &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj;'s space requirements and practicality if limited to the outer display, which faces away from the user when unfolded. Users might need to switch to &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj; when using the inner screen, or turn the device around to authenticate with &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj;, creating what the leaker suggested would be a disjointed experience.<br/>
<br/>
The comments fit an emerging picture of a relatively modest second-generation device, with more substantial changes potentially arriving with the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; 3. <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/15/apple-aims-to-upgrade-iphone-duo-in-four-ways/">said on Sunday</a> that Apple has developed &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; 2 prototypes with &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; on the outer display, but is running out of time to finalize the feature, meaning it could slip to the third generation.<br/>
<br/>
Apple this week introduced a more limited <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-face-unlock-hands-on/">Face Unlock option</a> for the existing &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; in iOS 27.3 beta 2. Called "Unlock with Front Camera," the feature uses the standard outer camera to unlock the device when closed. It does not provide the depth-sensing authentication of &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj;, cannot authorize <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-pay/">Apple Pay</a> purchases or autofill passwords, and still requires &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj; or a passcode when the device is unfolded.<br/>
<br/>
